WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.478
Northwind Logistics wants a loan for new equipment.

2
00:00:03.478 --> 00:00:08.997
A lender will ask for a year of bank statements, tax records, and the company's ownership.

3
00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:15.259
Northwind already proved who it is and who owns it, when it opened its bank account.

4
00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:17.579
That work does not need doing twice.

5
00:00:18.429 --> 00:00:23.463
Northwind asks its bank to keep a record of its cash flow up to date in the company's pod.

6
00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:26.763
The bank publishes the business's own data to the business.

7
00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:32.210
The state revenue department confirms that Northwind's tax filings are up to date.

8
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.513
The lender asks for four things: identity, ownership, tax status and cash flow.

9
00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:43.483
Northwind approves, for thirty days, for one purpose: a credit decision.

10
00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:47.672
The lender reads twelve months of cash flow at source.

11
00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:50.825
No statements are exported, and nothing is retyped.

12
00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:52.432
Each signature is checked.

13
00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:57.409
The decision, and the reasons for it, are written back to Northwind's pod.

14
00:00:58.259 --> 00:01:01.550
Loans like this come with conditions, checked every quarter.

15
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.648
Northwind grants the lender a quarterly read of its cash flow, for as long as the loan is open.

16
00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:10.576
The frequency and the end date are part of the grant.

17
00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:13.764
Three months on, the check is a read.

18
00:01:13.764 --> 00:01:15.659
Nobody prepares a certificate.

19
00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.968
When the loan is repaid, Northwind withdraws the grant, and the lender's next read is refused.

20
00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:29.218
Two issuers, one lender, one decision written back, and a monitoring arrangement the borrower could read and end.

21
00:01:30.068 --> 00:01:37.095
If you lend to small businesses, or supply data to those who do, join the EDMA Solid Community of Practice.
